  "user_request_original": "Design a 6-layer periodic quarter-wave dielectric stack on Ge substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: ZnS | ZnSe | ZnS | ZnSe | ZnS | ZnSe (6 finite layers). Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness centered at 9500 nm wavelength with bounds 500-2500 nm per layer. Optimize for high transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band and low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. Total layer count fixed at 6. Use normal incidence, unpolarized light. Verify all material optical constants are available across both wavelength bands before optimization. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
